. * ============================
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR 4 * 
. * ============================
. 
.         /* To test Hypotheses 4,  
>         assuming that daughters leads to stronger support for gender equality
>  for men than for women, 
>         we estimate a pooled ordinary least squares (POLS) regression models 
> with an interaction term. 
>         Specifically, we run the OLS with a standardized index of attitudes '
> genderatt_index' as dependent variable 
>         and the interaction between the dummy variable 'child_daugther' and r
> espondents' sex 'p_sex' as independent variable. */
.         
.         *H4
.         reg genderatt_index i.child_daugther##i.p_sex ///
>                 p_son kage_firfem c.p_age##c.p_age i.p_emp i.p_married i.p_co
> hab ///    // individual-level controls 
>                 ln_hhincome i.p_educ p_migback p_east p_mode i.p_sibl syear_1
> 2 ///                      // other 
>                 [pw=xrwght] , vce(cluster pid)  
